<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      DEFAULT (kscan.mwdat.enabled = false) MANIFEST — deliberately empty.

      This library is autolinked into EVERY K Scan Android build, flag or no
      flag, because it lives in modules/ and expo-modules-autolinking picks it
      up unconditionally. Whatever this file declares is therefore merged into
      the shipping app's manifest even when the DAT SDK was never compiled in.

      This file used to declare BLUETOOTH, BLUETOOTH_CONNECT, INTERNET, CAMERA
      and the DAT App Model meta-data. The merged debug manifest confirmed the
      result: a build with the flag OFF still requested BLUETOOTH and
      BLUETOOTH_CONNECT — a runtime "Nearby devices" permission on Android 12+
      — for hardware it has no code to talk to. Neither permission is declared
      anywhere else in K Scan, so both were contributed solely by this module,
      and both would have shipped to Play as a new sensitive-permission request
      on a feature users cannot even reach.

      The DAT requirements now live in src/mwdat/AndroidManifest.xml, selected
      by android/build.gradle only when the flag is on — the same gate that
      already controls the DAT source set and dependencies.
    -->

</manifest>
